# Text files keep LF line endings on every system (Git for Windows checks text out with CRLF by default): llama.cpp's
# patch has to match its LF source, and the build scripts run in bash.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Plan P3 (docs/implementation/python-free-plan.md §P3.3 + §P4): the product is Rust + JS.
# The contract suite and the fixture/notice generators stay Python ON PURPOSE — they are the
# gates and the raw material, a harness CI carries, never the shipping image. Marking them
# vendored makes GitHub's language bar read the product, and records the choice where a
# reader will look.
server/tests/** linguist-vendored
scripts/** linguist-vendored
